   "source": [
    "# Week 5: Pseudo-Labeling, Retraining & Ablation\n",
    "\n",
    "**Project**: Explainable Fake Review Detection for Bangla\n",
    "**Course**: CSE 4262 Data Analytics Lab\n",
    "\n",
    "This notebook implements Week 5:\n",
    "1. Load LR model (for calibrated probabilities) and BanglishRev data\n",
    "2. Generate pseudo-labels on BanglishRev with confidence > 0.90\n",
    "3. Audit pseudo-label distribution, calibration, class balance\n",
    "4. Combine gold train+val with accepted pseudo-labels\n",
    "5. Retrain all 5 models on expanded training set\n",
    "6. Ablation: gold-only vs gold+pseudo vs feature ablations\n",
    "7. Evaluate on validation set, select final model for test\n",
    "\n",
    "**Key Controls**:\n",
    "- Confidence threshold: 0.90 (configurable)\n",
    "- Pseudo-labels only enter TRAINING, never validation/test\n",
    "- Cap pseudo-label volume if it overwhelms gold data\n",
    "- Lower sample weights for pseudo-labeled rows\n",
    "- Sensitivity check at 0.95 threshold"
   ]
  },
